That works out to players mostly not using teleport except as an escape
mechanism, though; not really where I want to go since I'm wanting to
reintroduce teleport control as a more meaningful intrinsic post-Amulet.

> good?  I'm sort of aiming for the ability to use teleport to get out
> of trouble as a last resort without making it too easy to skip all of
> a level on the run (which I believe is why you're blocking teleport?).

In vanilla, you save all teleportation scrolls you find (and there are a
ton), and use a few cursed ones for specific purposes such as bypassing
Rodney's zoo, entering the Sanctum post-invocation, and some other such
stuff.  On the way back up, you use all the uncursed ones _and_ your MP
with ^T to bypass Gehennom almost completely.

This is what I'm blocking -- the player needs to have to walk back up
through Gehennom, rather than just traverse a few no-teleport levels.

